  "briefing": [
    "Bristol. Tuesday 10 March 2026. On the top floor of No. 31 Queen Square, a Georgian house on the north side of the square, are the offices of Nightjar: twenty-two people and a sleep and meditation app with a million listeners. Last Friday, 6 March, Nightjar was to be sold to Halcyon Health of San Francisco for £60 million.",
    "At ten past seven that Friday, the cleaner found Will Harding, 43, Nightjar’s co-founder and chief executive, dead at his desk. He had been struck on the head with the glass award from his shelf. His sports watch stopped finding his pulse at 21:34 the night before, Thursday 5 March.",
    "The police have arrested Joel Lacey, 29, Nightjar’s lead developer. At ten past six on Thursday the whole office heard him shout at Will: ‘If you sign it tomorrow, I’ll tell them myself!’ He left at 20:51 and ran home, as he does every Thursday. His running app says ten kilometres in fifty minutes, but the run took sixty-five: from 21:24 to 21:38 he sat on a bench in Queen Square, twenty metres from No. 31’s bike-store door. He’s on bail, and the police expect to charge him with murder.",
    "Will’s widow, Claire Harding, has hired you. ‘At twenty past nine Will messaged me: “Joel’s right. I’m not signing it.” Fourteen minutes later he was dead. Why would Joel kill the man who’d just agreed with him?’",
    "Fiona Brodie, Will’s co-founder, is running Nightjar now, and has given you the run of the office. Everyone who was there on Thursday is still in Bristol."
  ],
